": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205cd"], "topics": ["60e2fb7b66f9ce3f243b5116"], "concepts": ["617aaa24ef3fe65ad8e86d8b"], "question": {"text": "One of the points of intersection of the curves $y=1+3 x-2 x^2$ and $y=\\frac{1}{x}$ is $\\left(\\frac{1}{2}, 2\\right)$. Let the area of the region enclosed by these curves be $\\frac{1}{24}(l \\sqrt{5}+\\mathrm{m})-\\mathrm{n} \\log _{\\mathrm{e}}(1+\\sqrt{5})$, where $l, \\mathrm{~m}, \\mathrm{n} \\in \\mathbf{N}$. Then $l+\\mathrm{m}+\\mathrm{n}$ is equal to"}, "options": [{"id": "919d4e", "text": "29", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4a2ee0e063d92630cc"}, {"id": "296239", "text": "31", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4a2ee0e063d92630cd"}, {"id": "943739", "text": "30", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4a2ee0e063d92630ce"}, {"id": "1e69be", "text": "32", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4a2ee0e063d92630cf"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f4a2ee0e063d92630d0", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205cd"], "topics": ["60e2fb3d66f9ce3f243b4d65"], "concepts": ["620b7c94ffe80c18ac13f902"], "question": {"text": "The axis of a parabola is the line $y=x$ and its vertex and focus are in the first quadrant at distances $\\sqrt{2}$ and $2 \\sqrt{2}$ units from the origin, respectively. If the point $(1, \\mathrm{k})$ lies on the parabola, then a possible value of $k$ is :-"}, "options": [{"id": "ca86d2", "text": "$4$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4a2ee0e063d92630d1"}, {"id": "6bf33c", "text": "$9$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4a2ee0e063d92630d2"}, {"id": "ba028b", "text": "$3$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4a2ee0e063d92630d3"}, {"id": "973adf", "text": "$8$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4a2ee0e063d92630d4"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f4a2ee0e063d92630d5", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205cd"], "topics": ["60e2faac66f9ce3f243b4565"], "concepts": ["60e2fbbf66f9ce3f243b54a2"], "question": {"text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> be a variable point on the parabola <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;Then, the locus of the mid-point of the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> and the foot of the perpendicular drawn from the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> to the line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></math> is:"}, "options": [{"id": "569a84", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4a2ee0e063d92630d6"}, {"id": "9ffba3", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>(</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4a2ee0e063d92630d7"}, {"id": "6efc02", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4a2ee0e063d92630d8"}, {"id": "f5443e", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f4a2ee0e063d92630d9"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id